      "statement": "The Temple lay desecrated for three years and ten days (15 Chislev 145 – 25 Chislev 148), not three and a half years.",
      "layer": "evidence",
      "passage": null,
      "classification": "strongly_supported",
      "reasoning": "1 Maccabees gives both dates (15 Chislev 145; 25 Chislev 148), and Josephus's Antiquities says three years. Three sources give round figures that differ: Josephus's Jewish War \"three years and six months\" (which Montgomery takes as an accommodation to Daniel) and 2 Maccabees \"two years\" (2 Macc 10:3, perhaps counting from a different starting point). The dated account of 1 Maccabees is preferred because it supplies both termini; the other figures are recorded as counterevidence.",
